model 1
# Blockout's level, a hall with a room over it, a corridor and a second room on the ground floor,
# two doors, a window, a lamp and stairs from the hall up to the room over it, cut from one block so
# every cut works on one closed solid. Meters, the block's corner at the origin.
box 22 6.6 8
# The block over the corridor and the second room taken away, which leaves them one floor.
cut box 12.4 3.6 8.4 at 10 3.4 -0.2
# The hall, its ceiling the floor of the room over it, and that room, open to the sky.
cut box 9.6 3 7.6 at 0.2 0.2 0.2
cut box 9.6 3.6 7.6 at 0.2 3.4 0.2
# The corridor, its walls what is left where the block on either side is taken away, and the
# second room.
cut box 5.8 3.6 2 at 10 0.2 3
cut box 5.8 3.8 3 at 10 -0.2 -0.2
cut box 5.8 3.8 3 at 10 -0.2 5.2
cut box 5.8 3.6 7.6 at 16 0.2 0.2
# A hole in the hall's ceiling over the stairs from their third step, room for the head of one
# climbing them, a little wider than they are, so no step touches its side along a line.
cut box 1.4 0.6 4.2 at 0.2 3 2
# Floors up, ceilings down and every other face a wall, before the openings, whose sides are theirs.
select +y
material floor
select -y
material ceiling
slot rename default wall
# The door from the hall into the corridor, through the hall's east wall.
select box 9.8 0.2 0.2 9.8 3.2 7.8
cut door 1.2 2.2 3.8
material door
# The door from the corridor into the second room, through its west wall.
select box 16 0.2 0.2 16 3.4 7.8
cut door 1.2 2.2 3.8
material door
# A window in the second room's south wall.
select box 16 0.2 0.2 21.8 3.4 0.2
cut window 1.6 1.2 2.9 1
material window
# A lamp under the middle of the hall's ceiling, an emissive panel joined to it, which lights the
# hall where the room over it keeps the sun out.
union box 1.2 0.08 1.2 at 4.4 3.12 3.4
material lamp
slot emissive lamp 40000 36000 30000
# The stairs, sixteen steps of a fifth of a meter from the hall's floor to the room over it,
# joined into the level.
union stairs 16 0.2 0.3 1.2 at 0.2 0.2 1.4
material stairs
select none
